{"Title":"An Act relative to consumer protection on online automobile franchise transactions","BillNumber":"S150","DocketNumber":"SD619","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"BPC0","Name":"Brendan P. Crighton","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BPC0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T14:04:34.54"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"BPC0","Name":"Brendan P. Crighton","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BPC0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T14:04:34.54"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S150/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Crighton, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 150) of Brendan P. Crighton for legislation relative to certain online automobile franchise transactions.  Consumer Protection and Professional Licensure.","DocumentText":"\tSection 48 of Chapter 93 of the General Laws is hereby amended by inserting at the end thereof the following subsection:-\r\n\tL. This section shall not apply to a transaction for the sale of a new or used motor vehicle by a seller holding a Class 1 license pursuant to section 59 of chapter 140 in which the buyer signs by electronic means away from the seller’s place of business a written contract regarding the sale of a motor vehicle; provided, however, the seller shall give written notice at time of sale to the buyer that this section does not apply.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J17","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J17"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}